ctiveness Wellbeing at Work Learning & Development Remote Working Employment Index Interview Preparation Benchmark Your Salary Job Hunting Tips Making Your Salary Go Further Writing a Great CV Networking Career Planning Future of Work Mentorship All Topics Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Canada Singapore Malaysia Work HR & Recruitment Payroll Employee Jobs Jobseeker Jobseeker Employee Employer Share Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job Refer a friend Apply now Jobs Education & Training Casual Social Work Field Education Liaison Officer Casual Social Work Field Education Liaison Officer at Excelsia University College Pennant Hills, New South Wales 2120 , Australia • Casual AI Job Summary Field Educators must be eligible for full membership of the AASW. Minimum five years full-time post-qualifying practice experience. Must have full Australian Working Rights. Sign up or log in to analyse my fit Role Type On-site • Temporary • Casual • Qualified Description Casual opportunities commencing November 2026 Free onsite parking and close to public transport Be an integral part of Excelsia’s life-transforming global Christian learning community. About the Role Primary responsibilities include: To provide general oversight of the field education placement for specific students undertaking their social work field education placements. To consult with the Field Education Coordinator, Field Educator, and student/s about placement structure, learning goals and assessment processes. To provide support for students undertaking field education components of study which evaluates students’ ability to integrate theory and practice, critically reflect, understand and respond to diverse needs and situations within the placement setting. Selection Criteria Qualifications and Professional Standing: Field Educators must be eligible for full membership of the AASW. A minimum five years full-time post-qualifying practice experience. Experience in a higher education setting (or equivalent) would be an advantage. Essential: Respect the Christian mission of Excelsia University College. An understanding of current and emerging trends in Social Work. Technological literacy in a wide range of desktop applications to support reporting and analysis role requirements. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to communicate and work effectively and cooperatively with colleagues from diverse cultural, religious, gender and socio-economic backgrounds. Proven organisational skills with the ability to prioritise and meet deadlines. Full Australian Working Rights. About Us Excelsia University College was founded in 1983 as Australia’s first Christian arts college and, together with Indiana Wesleyan University, we are part of a global Christian learning community with big plans to take Christian higher education to the next level in Australia and the Asia-Pacific region for undergraduate and postgraduate students. This casual position is based in Pennant Hills. Learn more about why Excelsia is Great Place to Work ® Certified and why our staff love working at Excelsia here: https://greatplacetowork.com.au/companies/excelsia-college/ How to Apply If you meet the above criteria, you have a great opportunity to join our Christian community. Please provide your application with resume via this website. If you have any queries regarding the position or application process, please contact us via work@excelsia.edu.au. This position may be filled as soon as suitable applicants are found, so early applications are encouraged. Excelsia University College is a smoke free campus. Company Overview Excelsia contributes to making a better world through active participation in a life-transforming global Christian learning community. Apply now Share this job Refer a friend Copy link Twitter LinkedIn Facebook Report this job × Your reason Fraudulent or scam job posting Inappropriate or offensive content Misleading job description Duplicate job posting 